# Blaze of Glory lifts only the limit on how many it may block ("Does not allow ... a creature to block any creatures it would
# not normally be able to block", 2004 ruling). Bot1 attacks with Balduvian Bears and Aven Skirmisher (flying); Bot2's
# Ironroot Treefolk has no reach. Cast on it, the requirement (CR 509.1c) covers only the Bears: blocking the Bears alone is
# the one legal declaration, no block at all is refused, and blocking the flyer is refused. The spell cannot target an
# attacker's creature (it is not one a defending player controls); the cast on the Treefolk is the positive control.

